sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as Student
    participant CAP as Capture+noise
    participant WK as Worker
    participant E as AsrEngine
    participant G as Gap marker
    participant UI as Caption UI

    Note over S,UI: Lesson running · airplane mode · one session

    S->>CAP: mic permission granted, session starts
    CAP->>CAP: calibrate room noise floor (rolling min)

    loop Every utterance
        CAP->>CAP: VAD segments against calibrated floor<br/>merge gaps under 300ms
        CAP->>CAP: estimate SNR + guard checks<br/>(min duration · continuous energy · loop)

        alt SNR below threshold
            CAP-->>G: RawSegment { reason: snr_below_threshold }
            Note over CAP,UI: Decoder never invoked —<br/>cheapest way to avoid a hallucination
            G-->>UI: render GAP — "[ ? noisy ]"
        else SNR acceptable
            CAP->>WK: PCM 16k mono + hotwords
            WK->>E: transcribe(segment, opts)
            E-->>WK: text + word-level timestamps
            WK->>G: TranscriptSegment { words, gaps, snrDb, latencyMs }
            G->>G: Taglish pass (TL / EN / MIX)
            alt word confidence below threshold
                G-->>UI: render GAP — "[ ? ]"
                Note over G,UI: A confident wrong caption is<br/>worse than a visible gap
            else word acceptable
                G-->>UI: render WORD
            end
            G->>UI: append line (never auto-scroll past reader)
        end

        opt Student taps
            S->>UI: "I missed this"
            UI->>G: FlaggedSpan recorded
        end

        G-->>CAP: checkpoint segment to IndexedDB<br/>(battery may die later)
    end

    Note over CAP,UI: Main thread never blocks —<br/>flag button and HUD always respond
